","elder","elderly","geriatric","gerontologic","gerontological","long in the tooth","matured","of a certain age","old as Methuselah","on in years","over the hill","senior","superannuated","ivy-covered","preserved","wintry"],"antonyms":["fresh"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["nonstale","overstale","stale-dated","stale drunk","stale-grown","stalely","stale-mouthed","staleness","stale read","stale-smelling","stale-worn","stool pigeon","unstale"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stale#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3a033e68623921175c","definition":"Clear, free of dregs and lees; old and strong.","example":"The stronger Beere is divided into two parts (viz.) mild and stale; the first may ease a man of a drought, but the later is like water cast into a Smiths forge, and breeds more heartburning, and as rust eates into Iron, so overstale Beere gnawes auletholes in the entrales, or else my skill failes, and what I have written of it is to be held as a jest.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["fresh"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["nonstale","overstale","stale-dated","stale drunk","stale-grown","stalely","stale-mouthed","staleness","stale read","stale-smelling","stale-worn","stool pigeon","unstale"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stale#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:55c27c9df988bf0f0c","definition":"Fallow, in reference to land.","example":"Lime would do very little or no good on stale ploughed lands.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["fresh"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["nonstale","overstale","stale-dated","stale drunk","stale-grown","stalely","stale-mouthed","staleness","stale read","stale-smel