"synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["nonstale","overstale","stale-dated","stale drunk","stale-grown","stalely","stale-mouthed","staleness","stale read","stale-smelling","stale-worn","stool pigeon","unstale","antistaling","unstaled","unstaling"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stale#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d78444c727e108e88d","definition":"To become stale; to grow unpleasant from age.","example":"The Drink from that Time flattens and stales.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["nonstale","overstale","stale-dated","stale drunk","stale-grown","stalely","stale-mouthed","staleness","stale read","stale-smelling","stale-worn","stool pigeon","unstale","antistaling","unstaled","unstaling"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stale#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0a2e9ea43de28a73fb","definition":"To make stale; to age in order to clear and strengthen (a drink, especially beer).","example":"Stalyn, or make stale drynke, defeco.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["nonstale","overstale","stale-dated","stale drunk","stale-grown","stalely","stale-mouthed","staleness","stale read","stale-smelling","stale-worn","stool pigeon","unstale","antistaling","unstaled","unstaling"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stale#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0f8db99d030297d07f","definition":"A long, thin handle (of rakes, axes, etc.)","example":"In Case your Cask is a Butt,...have ready boiling...Water, which put in, and, with a long Stale and a little Birch fastened to its End, scrub the Bottom.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["handle","haft","helve","shaft","snath","the shaft of a scythe","stem"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["nonstale","overstale","stale-dated","stale drunk","stale-grown","stalely","stale-mouthed","staleness","stale read","stale-smelling","stale-worn","stool pigeon","unstale","antistaling","unstaled","unstaling","rakestale"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stale#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d202a21c7a71b10c46","definition":"One of the posts or uprights of a ladder.","example":"Stales, the staves, or risings of a ladder, or the staves of a rack in a stable.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["handle","haft","helve","shaft","snath","the shaft of a scythe","stem"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dialectal","register":"dialectal","wordFamily":["nonstale","overstale","stale-dated","stale drunk","stale-grown","stalely","stale-mouthed","staleness","stale read","stale-smelling","stale-worn","stool pigeon","unstale","antistaling","unstaled","unstaling","rakestale"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stale#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:75c19e16d05ae88bbc","definition":"One of the rungs on a ladder.","example":"To begin then: not long before this paragraph was written, P fell into doze, and dreamt, he saw Jacob's ladder with one foot standing on the earth, the other reaching up into heaven. Dukes, Marquisses, and other Peers, fancy represented to him, as standing on the upper stales; on the middle ones, Knights and Baronets, and under them, a train of Esquires and Gentlemen, reaching to the bottom.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["handle","haft","helve","shaft","snath","the shaft of a scythe","s